WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.834
And there is the president.

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:02.335
Let's listen in California.

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:03.603
I want to briefly speak about

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:04.104
what's happened

00:00:04.104 --> 00:00:05.338
to the Silicon Valley Bank

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:07.741
and signature bank today.

00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:08.808
Thanks to the quick action

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:10.143
of my administration over the past

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:11.311
few days,

00:00:11.311 --> 00:00:13.380
Americans can have confidence

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:15.782
that the banking system is safe.

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:17.117
Your deposits will be there

00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:18.585
when you need them.

00:00:18.585 --> 00:00:20.253
Small businesses across the country,

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:22.522
the deposit accounts of these banks

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:23.857
can breathe easier, knowing

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:25.525
they'll be able to pay their workers

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:27.293
and pay their bills.

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:28.561
And their hardworking employees

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:30.730
can breathe easier as well.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:31.498
Last week,

00:00:31.498 --> 00:00:32.132
when we learned

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:33.900
of the problems of the banks

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:34.701
and the impact

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:36.069
they could have on jobs

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:37.370
from small businesses

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:39.873
and the banking system, the overall

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:41.074
I instructed my team

00:00:41.074 --> 00:00:43.676
to act quickly to protect these interest.

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:45.779
They've done that. They've done that.

00:00:45.779 --> 00:00:47.247
On Friday,

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:48.748
the government regulator in charge,

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:49.449
the FDIC,

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:51.217
took control of

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:53.420
Silicon Valley banks assets,

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:54.821
and over the weekend,

00:00:54.821 --> 00:00:56.456
it took control of signature banks

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:57.524
assets.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.125
Treasury Secretary Yellen

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:00.160
and a team of banking

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:02.495
regulators have taken action,

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:03.863
immediate action.

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:05.165
And here are the highlights.

00:01:05.165 --> 00:01:06.199
First,

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:07.333
all customers

00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:08.334
who had deposits in

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:10.470
these banks can rest assured.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:12.572
Rest assured, they'll be protected

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:14.407
and they'll have access to their money.

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:16.443
As of today,

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:17.877
that includes small businesses

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:18.645
across the country.

00:01:18.645 --> 00:01:20.013
The bank there

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:21.581
and need to make payroll,

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:22.382
pay their bills

00:01:22.382 --> 00:01:24.184
and stay open for business.

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:25.485
No losses.

00:01:25.485 --> 00:01:26.820
And I know this is an important point.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.055
No losses will be borne by the taxpayer

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:30.723
And we repeat that.

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:33.093
No losses will be borne by the taxpayers.

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:34.994
Instead, the money will come from

00:01:34.994 --> 00:01:36.029
the fees

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:37.764
that banks pay into the deposit

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:39.299
insurance fund.

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:41.734
Because of the actions of that,

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:42.836
because of the actions

00:01:42.836 --> 00:01:44.737
that our regulators have already taken.

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:46.773
Every American should feel confident

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:48.374
their deposits will be there.

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:50.110
If and when they need them.

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:51.077
Second,

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:52.579
the management of these banks

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:54.247
will be fired

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:56.583
if the bank is taken over by the FDIC.

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:58.418
The people running the bank

00:01:58.418 --> 00:02:00.553
should not work there anymore.

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:02.956
Third, investors in the banks

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:05.325
will not be protected.

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:07.193
They knowingly took a risk,

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:08.261
and when the risk didn't

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:10.263
pay off, investors lose their money.

00:02:10.864 --> 00:02:12.932
That's how capitalism works.

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:13.867
And fourth,

00:02:13.867 --> 00:02:14.901
there are important questions

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:15.835
of how these banks

00:02:15.835 --> 00:02:16.870
got into the circumstance

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:18.371
in the first place.

00:02:18.438 --> 00:02:20.273
We must get the full accounting

00:02:20.273 --> 00:02:20.840
of what happened

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:21.875
and why

00:02:21.875 --> 00:02:23.209
those responsible

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:25.411
can be held accountable.

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:27.747
And my administration, no one in my room,

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.516
no one is above the law.

00:02:29.516 --> 00:02:30.550
And finally,

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:31.351
we must reduce

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:33.786
the risks of this happening again.

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:34.921
During the Obama-Biden

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:36.623
administration, we put in place

00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:38.658
a tough requirement on banks

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:39.492
like Silicon

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:41.828
Valley Bank and Signature Bank,

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:43.463
including the Dodd-Frank law,

00:02:43.463 --> 00:02:45.865
to make sure that the crisis we saw

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:48.334
in 2008 would not happen again.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.503
Unfortunately,

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:52.138
the last administration rolled back

00:02:52.138 --> 00:02:53.673
some of these requirements.

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:54.874
I'm going to ask Congress

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:56.075
and the banking regulators

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:56.709
to strengthen

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:58.411
the rules for banks

00:02:58.411 --> 00:02:59.579
to make it less likely

00:02:59.579 --> 00:03:00.713
this kind of bank failure

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:02.081
would happen again

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:03.650
and to protect American jobs and

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:04.551
small businesses.

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:07.320
Look, the bottom line is this

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:09.622
Americans can rest assured

00:03:09.622 --> 00:03:11.891
that our banking system is safe.

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:13.693
Your deposits are safe.

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:15.094
Let me also assure you,

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:17.096
we will not stop at this.

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:19.032
We'll do whatever is needed

00:03:19.032 --> 00:03:19.999
on top of all.

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:22.135
Let's also take a look at moment

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:23.036
to put the situation

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:24.571
in a broader context.

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:26.539
We've made strong economic progress

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:28.107
in the past two years.

00:03:28.107 --> 00:03:28.608
We've created

00:03:28.608 --> 00:03:30.810
more than 12 million new jobs,

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.145
more jobs in two years

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:34.013
than any president has ever created

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:36.449
in a single four year term.

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:39.652
Unemployment is below 4% for 14

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:41.154
straight months.

00:03:41.154 --> 00:03:43.256
Take-Home pay for workers is going up,

00:03:43.256 --> 00:03:44.824
especially for lower and middle

00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:46.292
income workers.

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:47.427
And we've seen record

00:03:47.427 --> 00:03:48.528
numbers of people apply

00:03:48.528 --> 00:03:50.063
to start new businesses.

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:52.098
More than 10 million of them.

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:54.234
More than 10 million applications

00:03:54.234 --> 00:03:55.435
over the last two years.

00:03:55.435 --> 00:03:56.970
Starting businesses.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:58.338
Now we need to keep the program

00:03:58.338 --> 00:03:59.906
this progress going.

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:01.241
That's what swift action

00:04:01.241 --> 00:04:02.408
that my administration over

00:04:02.408 --> 00:04:03.276
the past few years

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:05.778
is all about protecting depositors

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:08.114
protecting the banking system,

00:04:08.114 --> 00:04:09.515
protecting the economic gains

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:11.584
we made together for the American people.

00:04:12.185 --> 00:04:12.852
Thank you.

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:13.586
God bless you.

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:15.154
And may God protect our troops

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:15.989
in California.

00:04:15.989 --> 00:04:17.523
Mr.
President, what do you know right now

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:18.858
about why this happened?

00:04:18.858 --> 00:04:19.892
And can you assure Americans

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:21.327
that there won't be a ripple effect?

00:04:21.327 --> 00:04:21.961
Well, the president

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:23.463
there was some notable comments.

00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:25.031
One, addressing steps already

00:04:25.031 --> 00:04:26.499
taken by his administration.

00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:28.101
He says Americans can't have confidence

00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:29.802
that the banking system is saved.

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:30.937
Your deposits will be there

00:04:30.937 --> 00:04:31.504
when you need them.

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:32.238
That a step taken

00:04:32.238 --> 00:04:33.273
over the weekend,

00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:35.208
that by this morning, depositors

00:04:35.208 --> 00:04:36.409
will have access to their funds.

00:04:36.409 --> 00:04:37.744
Also notable, Erica,

00:04:37.744 --> 00:04:38.911
he says that no losses

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:40.380
will be borne by taxpayers.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:41.114
This can be covered

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:41.748
by fees

00:04:41.748 --> 00:04:42.548
paid into the system

00:04:42.548 --> 00:04:45.084
by banks and bank leaders.

00:04:45.118 --> 00:04:46.953
The president said will be fired.

00:04:46.953 --> 00:04:48.721
Yeah, absolutely.

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:49.589
Let's bring in now

00:04:49.589 --> 00:04:51.157
senior White House correspondent M.J.

00:04:51.157 --> 00:04:52.558
Lee, CNN business

00:04:52.558 --> 00:04:53.960
chief business correspondent

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:55.028
Christine Romans.

00:04:55.028 --> 00:04:55.862
So, Christine, starting

00:04:55.862 --> 00:04:56.896
let's pick up

00:04:56.896 --> 00:04:57.530
because I heard you

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:59.132
as we were both furiously

00:04:59.132 --> 00:04:59.999
scribbling notes here

00:04:59.999 --> 00:05:01.501
as we were listening to the president.

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:03.670
The fact that he did point out

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:06.506
management will be fired here, saying,

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:07.540
listen, if they were at the helm

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:08.107
when this happened,

00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:10.209
they don't deserve to be here now. Yeah.

00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:11.411
And they made some big mistakes,

00:05:11.411 --> 00:05:12.645
it looks like in hindsight, right,

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:13.112
when they didn't

00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:15.114
manage their interest rate risk properly.

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:16.115
This is a company that

00:05:16.115 --> 00:05:17.550
took in a lot of money

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:18.284
in deposits

00:05:18.284 --> 00:05:19.152
for many, many years

00:05:19.152 --> 00:05:20.553
and put those deposits

00:05:20.553 --> 00:05:22.322
into long dated treasuries.

00:05:22.322 --> 00:05:24.290
And then as interest rates rose

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:26.059
those became less valuable.

00:05:26.059 --> 00:05:27.160
And at the same time,

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:28.361
when people started taking the

00:05:28.361 --> 00:05:29.128
deposits out

00:05:29.128 --> 00:05:31.531
because the tech sector had turned,

00:05:31.531 --> 00:05:33.199
then suddenly there was this mismatch

00:05:33.199 --> 00:05:34.167
for for this bank.

00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:35.835
And as they tried to raise money,

00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:37.403
they raised actually alarms

00:05:37.403 --> 00:05:38.671
that they were in trouble.

00:05:38.671 --> 00:05:40.506
And then you had a run on the bank.

00:05:40.506 --> 00:05:42.408
So that management is out.

00:05:42.408 --> 00:05:43.209
Christine, I have to ask you,

00:05:43.209 --> 00:05:44.677
because this is a first step

00:05:44.677 --> 00:05:45.645
and I heard from a lot of folks

00:05:45.645 --> 00:05:46.446
this weekend saying

00:05:46.446 --> 00:05:47.180
the administration

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:49.349
has to step in now to guarantee all

00:05:49.882 --> 00:05:51.484
even uninsured deposits.

00:05:51.484 --> 00:05:53.853
Of course,
because the FDIC, FDIC limits

00:05:53.853 --> 00:05:55.621
to $250,000.

00:05:55.621 --> 00:05:56.356
Many banks,

00:05:56.356 --> 00:05:57.523
big, big VC firms,

00:05:57.523 --> 00:05:58.558
but also small businesses

00:05:58.558 --> 00:06:00.960
have far more money in their accounts.

00:06:01.194 --> 00:06:03.463
Biden says we will not stop at this.

00:06:03.463 --> 00:06:05.732
We will do whatever is needed.

00:06:05.732 --> 00:06:06.566
Notable as well.

00:06:06.566 --> 00:06:07.900
What does that mean exactly?

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:09.736
What additional steps?

00:06:09.736 --> 00:06:12.071
Was he opening up to, if necessary?

00:06:12.305 --> 00:06:13.906
Well, he talked about more regulation

00:06:13.906 --> 00:06:15.441
to make sure this doesn't happen again.

00:06:15.441 --> 00:06:16.509
And I think that's really important.

00:06:16.509 --> 00:06:18.411
We have Dodd-Frank banking reforms

00:06:18.411 --> 00:06:20.079
after the last financial crisis

00:06:20.079 --> 00:06:22.382
and there had been lobbying and in 2018

00:06:22.415 --> 00:06:24.684
a loosening of some of those for banks

00:06:24.684 --> 00:06:25.718
just like this one.

00:06:25.718 --> 00:06:26.619
So I think there's

00:06:26.619 --> 00:06:27.620
going to be a postmortem

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:29.155
look at whether these kinds of banks

00:06:29.155 --> 00:06:30.323
should all have better stress

00:06:30.323 --> 00:06:31.591
tests tests

00:06:31.591 --> 00:06:34.394
and have a higher capital requirements.

00:06:34.394 --> 00:06:36.729
So that's a conversation to have.

00:06:36.729 --> 00:06:37.430
But this is just

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:39.031
such a unique moment overall.

00:06:39.031 --> 00:06:40.333
I mean do you want the federal government

00:06:40.333 --> 00:06:42.902
guaranteeing every investment

00:06:42.902 --> 00:06:44.303
every bank deposit

00:06:44.303 --> 00:06:46.472
and then you're essentially nationalizing

00:06:46.472 --> 00:06:47.206
the banks here.

00:06:47.206 --> 00:06:48.374
So I think it's important

00:06:48.374 --> 00:06:50.877
to note that in normal times $250,000

00:06:51.344 --> 00:06:52.311
or less your

00:06:52.311 --> 00:06:54.414
your deposits are guaranteed

00:06:54.414 --> 00:06:55.515
by the federal government.

00:06:55.515 --> 00:06:56.449
In this case,

00:06:56.449 --> 00:06:57.216
they're guaranteeing

00:06:57.216 --> 00:06:58.684
all of those deposits.

00:06:58.684 --> 00:07:00.186
That's a really new moment.

00:07:00.186 --> 00:07:01.854
And to get to that point,

00:07:01.854 --> 00:07:02.622
the president said

00:07:02.622 --> 00:07:03.856
he's going to be asking Congress

00:07:03.856 --> 00:07:04.891
to strengthen those rules.

00:07:04.891 --> 00:07:05.658
We heard from lawmakers

00:07:05.658 --> 00:07:06.926
on both sides of the aisle

00:07:06.926 --> 00:07:09.061
weighing in over the weekend.

00:07:09.061 --> 00:07:10.830
Is there a plan from the White House?

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:11.497
Is there a plan

00:07:11.497 --> 00:07:12.565
even from the president

00:07:12.565 --> 00:07:15.134
to speak to lawmakers

00:07:15.134 --> 00:07:16.402
and to get a sense of what

00:07:16.402 --> 00:07:18.137
that would look like when you're dealing,

00:07:18.137 --> 00:07:20.072
of course, with a divided Congress?

00:07:20.072 --> 00:07:20.673
Yeah, Erica,

00:07:20.673 --> 00:07:22.742
I thought the president accountable

00:07:23.176 --> 00:07:25.344
portion of the speech was really notable.

00:07:25.711 --> 00:07:27.146
First and foremost, the president

00:07:27.146 --> 00:07:28.080
saying straight up

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:29.582
that the managers

00:07:29.582 --> 00:07:31.784
at these banks are going to be fired

00:07:31.951 --> 00:07:33.119
and that the people

00:07:33.119 --> 00:07:35.121
who are responsible for what happen,

00:07:35.488 --> 00:07:37.557
they're going to be held accountable now.

00:07:37.557 --> 00:07:38.891
We don't know what exactly

00:07:38.891 --> 00:07:40.593
that accountability looks like.

00:07:40.593 --> 00:07:41.661
And he made clear

00:07:41.661 --> 00:07:43.196
that there is going to be

00:07:43.196 --> 00:07:44.130
a little bit of time

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:45.932
that is taken to figure out

00:07:45.932 --> 00:07:46.632
and get a full

00:07:46.632 --> 00:07:48.000
accounting of what

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:50.303
led to these banks failures.

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:52.705
But I think just in the big picture,

00:07:52.705 --> 00:07:54.307
yes, the president is

00:07:54.307 --> 00:07:55.308
going to be speaking

00:07:55.308 --> 00:07:56.509
to members of Congress.

00:07:56.509 --> 00:07:57.310
You would expect

00:07:57.310 --> 00:07:58.077
that there are going to be

00:07:58.077 --> 00:07:59.312
these kinds of conversations

00:07:59.312 --> 00:08:01.080
sort of looking back

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:02.348
at the last few years.

00:08:02.348 --> 00:08:03.683
Some of the relaxation

00:08:03.683 --> 00:08:05.051
of some of these regulations

00:08:05.051 --> 00:08:06.118
over the last few years

00:08:06.118 --> 00:08:07.453
to try to figure out

00:08:07.453 --> 00:08:09.422
what how can we actually prevent

00:08:09.422 --> 00:08:11.791
this kind of thing from happening again.

00:08:11.791 --> 00:08:13.326
But I think for this morning,

00:08:13.326 --> 00:08:14.460
at this moment,

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:15.661
it was very important

00:08:15.661 --> 00:08:16.629
for the White House.

00:08:16.629 --> 00:08:18.064
Remember, these remarks were added

00:08:18.064 --> 00:08:19.565
at the very last minute,

00:08:19.565 --> 00:08:20.633
late last night

00:08:20.633 --> 00:08:22.068
for the president to get out there.

00:08:22.068 --> 00:08:23.035
In front of the cameras

00:08:23.035 --> 00:08:25.104
and directly address the American people

00:08:25.238 --> 00:08:26.272
and say this lying,

00:08:26.272 --> 00:08:26.973
which was key,

00:08:26.973 --> 00:08:29.275
he said the banking system is safe.

00:08:29.408 --> 00:08:30.209
Your does

00:08:30.209 --> 00:08:32.011
your deposits will be there

00:08:32.011 --> 00:08:33.446
when you need them.

00:08:33.446 --> 00:08:34.981
He really wanted to sort of reassure

00:08:34.981 --> 00:08:35.915
the American people,

00:08:35.915 --> 00:08:37.216
you know, many of whom

00:08:37.216 --> 00:08:38.518
obviously have

00:08:38.518 --> 00:08:40.920
recollections going back to the 2008

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:42.121
financial crisis.

00:08:42.121 --> 00:08:43.623
That that is not the scenario

00:08:43.623 --> 00:08:44.690
that we are about to see that

00:08:44.690 --> 00:08:45.958
there's not going to be

00:08:45.958 --> 00:08:47.193
some domino effect.

00:08:47.193 --> 00:08:48.261
And by the way,

00:08:48.261 --> 00:08:49.262
he took a lot of credit

00:08:49.262 --> 00:08:50.563
for what he called were

00:08:50.563 --> 00:08:52.265
immediate and quick actions

00:08:52.265 --> 00:08:54.267
by his administration last night

00:08:54.267 --> 00:08:55.835
to prevent that kind of scenario

00:08:55.835 --> 00:08:56.836
from happening.

00:08:56.836 --> 00:08:57.904
Well, a message to the public

00:08:57.904 --> 00:08:59.372
certainly also a message to the markets

00:08:59.372 --> 00:09:00.406
that opened in 20 minutes.

00:09:00.406 --> 00:09:01.874
Now watching those comments

00:09:01.874 --> 00:09:03.376
I'm sure very closely. M.J.

00:09:03.376 --> 00:09:03.943
Lee at the White House.

00:09:03.943 --> 00:09:05.111
Christine Romans, thanks so much.

